# Route additions for client/src/App.tsx

Add this lazy import near the top of `App.tsx` with the other lazy page imports:

```tsx
const LeadGenAdmin = lazy(() => import("./pages/admin/lead-gen"));
```

Add this route inside the `AdminRoute`-protected section (wherever the other
`/admin/*` routes are — the wrapper will handle auth gating):

```tsx
<Route path="/admin/lead-gen/:rest*">
  <AdminRoute>
    <LeadGenAdmin />
  </AdminRoute>
</Route>
```

Note: use `:rest*` (wouter wildcard) so all nested tabs under /admin/lead-gen
(leads, campaigns, templates, settings) route through the layout component's
internal `<Switch>`.

If your existing admin route looks different (e.g. already uses a `/admin/*`
catch-all with a nested router), just add `LeadGenAdmin` to that inner
router's route table instead.
